# Trees tools/mermaid-lint.sh leaves alone. One path per line; a line
# matching no tracked file fails the run.
#
# Every line here also needs the matching '!path/**' on both of the
# paths lists in .github/workflows/mermaid-lint.yml. The script reads
# this file and GitHub Actions cannot, so the two halves are kept in
# step by hand -- and they have to be, because the script lints the
# whole tree on every run. A path the workflow skips but the script
# still reads fails somebody else's pull request over a diagram they
# did not write.

# An automated import of the sibling repositories' documentation,
# refreshed hourly by sync-external-docs.yml with no local review.
# AGENTS.md forbids editing it here -- a diagram broken in instar,
# kerbside, ryll or occystrap is fixed in the repository it came from,
# where the sibling's own mermaid lane is what catches it. 664 of this
# repository's 918 tracked markdown files live here, so linting them
# would also spend most of the lane on content that is not ours.
docs/components
